<p style="text-align: center;">The Meadow. 5x7, oil on linen panel. 2016</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Following on from my <a href="http://www.portraitsbysimonbland.com/blog/post/preparing-linen-a-short-how-to-guide" target="_blank">previous post</a> on making your own canvas. Before starting any kind of substantial painting on a new linen, I think it's a good idea to try it out and see how it performs. This afternoon I did a small painting to test it out.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Overall, the linen has a fairly substantial texture. This lends itself to a heavier paint application, something that I usually try to avoid. Based on this experience I added an extra layer of primer to most the panels I'd already made from the linen.</p>